    accTitle: Coaching, Mentoring, and Feedback
    accDescr: Coaching, mentoring, and feedback are related but distinct. Coaching is ongoing, centered on a goal the person themselves defines, unfolding over months toward a broader development trajectory. Mentoring is in-the-moment and problem-specific, building technical judgment. Feedback is close to a specific, recent instance, correcting or reinforcing behavior. Coaching often uses mentoring and feedback as tools within a broader coaching relationship, rather than being separate, unrelated practices.
